{"type": "message", "id": "d6da6eeb", "parentId": "ed1fccdc", "timestamp": "2026-04-08T19:27:17.218Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "toolu_bdrk_017bXUVHL6Ny1s1juFj7gnyh", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"Nation's Report Card 2022 grade 8 math scores by state average\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 1007,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c03ebdf999779cb6\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c03ebdf999779cb6\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"34ad069fcd46777f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe table below shows the number of states/jurisdictions with score increases or decreases in 2022 and how many states/jurisdictions scored higher, lower, or not significantly different than the nation (public) in NAEP mathematics.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"34ad069fcd46777f\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"dd45929e6377a7b0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT NATION  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"dd45929e6377a7b0\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011NP8.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"38fa7eed0de96715\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n• In 2022, male students in the nation had an average score that was higher than that ... NOTE: <strong>The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from 0 t