74</strong> in 2022 – a decline of 8 points\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b93f973c34ccb039\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"October 24, 2022\",\n      \"siteName\": \"whiteboardadvisors.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fd5dff8275e51b81\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nElementary and Secondary STEM Education | NSF - National Science Foundation\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fd5dff8275e51b81\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ncses.nsf.gov/pubs/nsb202331/table/K12-1\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e6a7be7a75d8149c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAverage NAEP mathematics scores in 2022 for students in eighth grade ranged from <strong>259 to 284</strong> (Figure K12-8). Students in New Mexico, the District of Columbia, and West Virginia had the lowest average scores, whereas students in Massachusetts, Utah, and Idaho had average scores that were higher ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e6a7be7a75d8149c\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"October 26, 2023\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ncses.nsf.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5b5381bcc6bd2fb6\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNOVEMBER 2022\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5b5381bcc6bd2fb6\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://csgsouth.org/wp-content/uploads/QofM-November.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"86798c639018857e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nProcess (NAEP). 2022 Mathematics Assessment. The decline in mathematics scores in the eighth grade is more significant, as 10 states fell below the national average · (274). Virginia (279) was the only state to score above the national average.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"86798c639018857e\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"csgsouth.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"55c9d97fc50bf01f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2024 National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP)\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"55c9d97fc50bf01f\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.cde.state.co.us/assessment/summary-of-facts-2024-naep-math-grades-4-and-8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"24e7c055730894e2\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe percentage of students in Colorado ... or above NAEP Basic in 2024 (77 percent) was · greater than that in 1992 (61 percent) and was not significantly different from that in 2022 (75 percent). ... In 2024, the average mathematics scale score for eighth-grade students in Colorado was 278...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"24e7c055730894e2\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"January 2, 2024\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.cde.state.co.us\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "NAEP 2022 grade 8 math Kansas score 278 OR 279 OR 280 OR 281 OR 282", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 877, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"597a185d6760c0b0\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2022 National Assessment of Educational Progress Grade 8 Mathematics Results\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"597a185d6760c0b0\">>>", "url": "https://www.fldoe.org/core/fileparse.php/7667/urlt/2022NAEPGrade8Math.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4523d1c25382fede\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNOTE: <strong>The NAEP Mathematics scale ranges from 0 to 500</strong>. Observed differences are not necessarily statistically significant. Basic · Proficient · Advanced · Page 10 · 266 · 275 · 282 283 · 288 288 · 280 · 287 · 272 · 268 · 273 275 · 281 281 279 282 · 277 · 268 · 274 277 · 279 ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4523d1c25382fede\">>>", "siteName": "www.fldoe.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"94398e914fa3a905\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nAnalysis of 2022 NAEP Mathematics and Reading Results\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"94398e914fa3a905\">>>", "url": "https://whiteboardadvisors.com/analysis-of-2022-naep-mathematics-and-reading-results/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b93f973c34ccb039\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nAverage eighth grade math score fell from 282 in 2019 to <strong>274</strong> in 2022 – a decline of 8 points\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b93f973c34ccb039\">>>", "published": "October 24, 2022", "siteName": "whiteboardadvisors.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"fd5dff8275e51b81\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nElementary and Secondary STEM Education | NSF - National Science Foundation\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"fd5dff8275e51b81\">>>", "url": "https://ncses.nsf.gov/pubs/nsb202331/table/K12-1", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e6a7be7a75d8149c\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nAverage NAEP mathematics scores in 2022 for students in eighth grade ranged from <strong>259 to 284</strong> (Figure K12-8). Students in New Mexico, the District of Columbia, and West Virginia had the lowest average scores, whereas students in Massachusetts, Utah, and Idaho had average scores that were higher ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e6a7be7a75d8149c\">>>", "published": "October 26, 2023", "siteName": "ncses.nsf.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5b5381bcc6bd2fb6\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNOVEMBER 2022\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5b5381bcc6bd2fb6\">>>", "url": "https://csgsouth.org/wp-content/uploads/QofM-November.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"86798c639018857e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nProcess (NAEP). 2022 Mathematics Assessment. The decline in mathematics scores in the eighth grade is more significant, as 10 states fell below the national average · (274). Virginia (279) was the only state to score above the national average.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"86798c639018857e\">>>", "siteName": "csgsouth.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"55c9d97fc50bf01f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2024 National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP)\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"55c9d97fc50bf01f\">>>", "url": "https://www.cde.state.co.us/assessment/summary-of-facts-2024-naep-math-grades-4-and-8", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"24e7c055730894e2\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe percentage of students in Colorado ... or above NAEP Basic in 2024 (77 percent) was · greater than that in 1992 (61 percent) and was not significantly different from that in 2022 (75 percent). ... In 2024, the average mathematics scale score for eighth-grade students in Colorado was 278...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"24e7c055730894e2\">>>", "published": "January 2, 2024", "siteName": "www.cde.state.co.us"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1775676513024}}
