{"type": "message", "id": "9ab36710", "parentId": "7e04356d", "timestamp": "2026-04-08T19:28:41.461Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "toolu_bdrk_01N6Swo8cF6kxkfQPYbq7cR4", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"NAEP 2022 grade 8 mathematics \\\"South Carolina\\\" average score\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 885,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c103a14a3d48387b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNational, South Carolina 2022 NAEP Results Released - South Carolina Department of Education - 05/17/2025 7:37 PM\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c103a14a3d48387b\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ed.sc.gov/newsroom/news-releases/national-south-carolina-2022-naep-results-released/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d69c219f50239d1f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSouth Carolina eighth-graders’ average score was <strong>269</strong> compared to 276 in 2019 and 275 in 2017. The average national score for public schools in 2022 was 273, an 8-point drop from 2019.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d69c219f50239d1f\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"October 24, 2022\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ed.sc.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"820feb523cc8d427\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 Mathematics Snapshot Report: South Carolina Grade 8\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"820feb523cc8d427\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011SC8.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"73a60afbca19be54\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNOTE: The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from <strong>0 to 500</strong>. Results presented in this report are based on public school students only.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"73a60afbca19be54\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b887a8118389c6fb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 Reading Snapshot Report: South Carolina Grade 8\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b887a8118389c6fb\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023010SC8.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c45fb96c82cdec50\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP is an educational assessment. Often called The Nation&#x27;s Report Card, it provides national, state, and district-level results about students&#x27; academic achievement.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c45fb96c82cdec50\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9c7256172d52d62e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Files - South Carolina Department of Education - 05/22/2025 1:19 AM\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9c7256172d52d62e\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ed.sc.gov/tests/tests-files/naep-files/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1f1da94eeb3be323\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIt is the largest nationally representative and continuing assessment of what our nation’s students know and can do in various subjects such as civics, mathematics, reading, and U.S. history. The program also provides valuable insights into students’ educational experiences and opportunities to learn in and outside of the classroom. NAEP is a congressionally mandated program administered by the National Center for Education Statistics (NCES), within the U.S. Department of Education and the Institute of Education Sciences. NAEP Fall 2023 Facts for Districts: Grades 4, 8, and 12 Field Test\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1f1da94eeb3be323\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ed.sc.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"150bff054e5d41bc\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 Mathematics Snapshot Report: South Carolina Grade 8\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"150bff054e5d41bc\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ed.sc.gov/tests/tests-files/naep-files/2022-one-page-snapshot-report-grade-8-math/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"70285b2fff3273c8\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNational Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP):\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"70285b2fff3273c8\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ed.sc.gov\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "NAEP 2022 grade 8 mathematics \"South Carolina\" average score", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 885, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c103a14a3d48387b\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNational, South Carolina 2022 NAEP Results Released - South Carolina Department of Education - 05/17/2025 7:37 PM\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c103a14a3d48387b\">>>", "url": "https://ed.sc.gov/newsroom/news-releases/national-south-carolina-2022-naep-results-released/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d69c219f50239d1f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nSouth Carolina eighth-graders’ average score was <strong>269</strong> compared to 276 in 2019 and 275 in 2017. The average national score for public schools in 2022 was 273, an 8-point drop from 2019.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d69c219f50239d1f\">>>", "published": "October 24, 2022", "siteName": "ed.sc.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"820feb523cc8d427\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2022 Mathematics Snapshot Report: South Carolina Grade 8\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRU