{"type": "message", "id": "8a420f95", "parentId": "15d91d56", "timestamp": "2026-04-08T19:28:49.425Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "toolu_bdrk_011CHVC32hjBMSWvbwQ5xWcw", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"NAEP 2022 grade 8 mathematics Kentucky average score\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 979,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"911edcd554299c3f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT KENTUCKY  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"911edcd554299c3f\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011KY8.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"dc445886a7085251\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNOTE: Puerto Rico was not included in the comparison results. AVERAGE SCORES FOR STATE/JURISDICTION AND THE NATION (PUBLIC) ... White students. This performance gap was not significantly different from that in 2000 ... NOTE: The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from <strong>0 to 500</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"dc445886a7085251\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4f843563942b5736\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4f843563942b5736\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"aea2e144ab7f653d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n... In the 43 states/jurisdictions where scores were lower in 2022 than 2019, the size of the score differences ranged from 2 to <strong>14 points</strong>. The average score decline for public schools in the nation decreased by 5 points. To view score changes for fourth-grade public school students in mathematics ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"aea2e144ab7f653d\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"27bb6928b2d8a9b6\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNOVEMBER 2022\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"27bb6928b2d8a9b6\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://csgsouth.org/wp-content/uploads/QofM-November.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e60df2b24db5a982\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nOn October 24, 2022, the United States Department of Education’s National Center for Education Statistics (NCES) released the results of the National Assessment of Education Progress (NAEP) – commonly referred to as “The Nation’s · Report Card.” Due to the pandemic’s impact, the national average scores in mathematics for fourth- and eighth-graders\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e60df2b24db5a982\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"csgsouth.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2e0dab86ea4cb585\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: Mathematics Highlights 2022\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2e0dab86ea4cb585\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bb8e67bfd4b47f9b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe average eighth-grade mathematics score <strong>decreased by 8 points compared to 2019</strong> and was lower than all previous assessment years going back to 2003. In 2022, fourth- and eighth-grade mathematics scores declined for most states/jurisdictions as well as for most participating urban districts ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bb8e67bfd4b47f9b\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"af4d82bd8cbbc3f4\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nKentucky’s 2022 National Assessment of Educational Progress results released\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"af4d82bd8cbbc3f4\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.kentuckyteacher.org/news/2022/10/kentuckys-2022-national-assessment-of-educational-progress-results-released/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"65219fc043ae8e33\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe results of the 2022 National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP), also known as the Nation’s Report Card, were release on Oct. 24. The results show Kentucky’s public school students’ NAEP performance is consistent with those of the rest of the nation.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"65219fc043ae8e33\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"October 24, 2022\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.kentuckyteacher.org\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "NAEP 2022 grade 8 mathematics Kentucky average score", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 979, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"911edcd554299c3f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT KENTUCKY  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"911edcd554299c3f\">>>", "url": "https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011KY8.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"dc445886a7085251\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNOTE: Puerto Rico was not included in the comparison results. AVERAGE SCORES FOR STATE/JURISDICTION AND THE NATION (PUBLIC) ... White students. This performance gap was not significantly different from that in 2000 ... NOTE: The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from <strong>0 to 500</strong>.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"dc445886a7085251\">>>", "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4f843563942b5736\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4f843563942b5736\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"aea2e144ab7f653d\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n... In the 43 states/jurisdictions where scores were lower in 2022 than 2019, the size of the score differences ranged from 2 to <strong>14 points</strong>. The average score decline for public schools in the nation decreased by 5 points. To view score changes for fourth-grade public school students in mathematics ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"aea2e144ab7f653d\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"27bb6928b2d8a9b6\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNOVEMBER 2022\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"27bb6928b2d8a9b6\">>>", "url": "https://csgsouth.org/wp-content/uploads/QofM-November.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e60df2b24db5a982\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nOn October 24, 2022, the United States Department of Education’s National Center for Education Statistics (NCES) released the results of the National Assessment of Education Progress (NAEP) – commonly referred to as “The Nation’s · Report Card.” Due to the pandemic’s impact, the national average scores in mathematics for fourth- and eighth-graders\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e60df2b24db5a982\">>>", "siteName": "csgsouth.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2e0dab86ea4cb585\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: Mathematics Highlights 2022\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2e0dab86ea4cb585\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"bb8e67bfd4b47f9b\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe average eighth-grade mathematics score <strong>decreased by 8 points compared to 2019</strong> and was lower than all previous assessment years going back to 2003. In 2022, fourth- and eighth-grade mathematics scores declined for most states/jurisdictions as well as for most participating urban districts ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"bb8e67bfd4b47f9b\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"af4d82bd8cbbc3f4\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nKentucky’s 2022 National Assessment of Educational Progress results released\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"af4d82bd8cbbc3f4\">>>", "url": "https://www.kentuckyteacher.org/news/2022/10/kentuckys-2022-national-assessment-of-educational-progress-results-released/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"65219fc043ae8e33\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe results of the 2022 National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP), also known as the Nation’s Report Card, were release on Oct. 24. The results show Kentucky’s public school students’ NAEP performance is consistent with those of the rest of the nation.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"65219fc043ae8e33\">>>", "published": "October 24, 2022", "siteName": "www.kentuckyteacher.org"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1775676529425}}
