{"type": "message", "id": "eee1013f", "parentId": "aff80f70", "timestamp": "2026-04-08T19:30:26.200Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "toolu_bdrk_01TCot7SdeSGaZutvtP1pnjY", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"Arizona 2024 NAEP snapshot math grade 8 \\\"in 2022\\\" score\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 888,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bb1114a999d51b79\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP State and District Snapshots\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bb1114a999d51b79\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/snapshots/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"621aa2450f863047\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nExplore and download state and district snapshots of NAEP data in mathematics, reading, science, and writing.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"621aa2450f863047\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"October 10, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"acba8b0ab493da21\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe New NAEP Scores Highlight a Standards Gap in Many States - FutureEd\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"acba8b0ab493da21\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.future-ed.org/the-new-naep-scores-highlight-a-standards-gap-in-many-states/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3d9fb0da02b9b657\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nForty-seven states improved NAEP math proficiency rates between 2022 and 2024 in fourth grade and 36 states did so in eighth grade. But proficiency rates remain below 2019 levels in 34 states in fourth-grade and in all but one state in eighth-grade. Similarly, math proficiency rates rose on nearly every state’s standardized tests during the same period. While state math scores declined dramatically between 2019 and 2022, particularly in eighth grade, only in Arizona, Arkansas, Florida, Idaho, and Vermont in fourth grade and Arkansas, Michigan, and Missouri in eighth grade did state test scores decline between 2022 and 2024.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3d9fb0da02b9b657\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 10, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.future-ed.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0003f6835338c3fb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0003f6835338c3fb\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"198952e6e3f6d0cd\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTo compare average mathematics scores between states/jurisdictions and the nation (public), use the NAEP State Profiles Tool. ... In the 43 states/jurisdictions where scores were lower in 2022 than 2019, <strong>the size of the score differences ranged from 2 to 14 points</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"198952e6e3f6d0cd\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a31bf7cf4f0a3578\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: Mathematics Highlights 2022\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a31bf7cf4f0a3578\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0b3688646cc736ee\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn 2022, the average fourth-grade mathematics score decreased by 5 points and was lower than all previous assessment years going back to 2005; the average score was one point higher compared to 2003. The average eighth-grade mathematics score <strong>decreased by 8 points compared to 2019 and was lower</strong> ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0b3688646cc736ee\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d9dba0123c2afcf5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: Performance Trends for States and Districts\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d9dba0123c2afcf5\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/reports/mathematics/2024/g4_8/state-district-trends/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c1cc6796571967a5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n... NOTE: DS = Department of Defense ... a higher percentage of students performing at or above NAEP Proficient in mathematics in 2024, <strong>increases ranged from 1 to 10 percentage points</strong>....\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c1cc6796571967a5\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "Arizona 2024 NAEP snapshot math grade 8 \"in 2022\" score", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 888, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"bb1114a999d51b79\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP State and District Snapshots\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"bb1114a999d51b79\">>>", "url": "https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/snapshots/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"621aa2450f863047\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nExplore and download state and district snapshots of NAEP data in mathematics, reading, science, and writing.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"621aa2450f863047\">>>", "published": "October 10, 2025", "siteName": "nces.ed.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"acba8b0ab493da21\"